From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: punktfunk <packages@unom.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] pipewire: write NVIDIA's planar capture into a buffer

With 0035 a GTX 1080 Ti still streamed the NV12 capture striped: 32-byte
sectors moved inside each KiB. An EGL import, a map of the allocation's own
memory object and a Vulkan buffer import all read the same scramble, so the
bytes already sat off the LINEAR layout the export names when the storage
image stores into the LINEAR NV12 image wrote them. On the same card, a
Vulkan pass that fills a storage buffer word by word reads back clean.

On NVIDIA, back a planar capture with an exportable storage buffer: luma
rows, then chroma rows at the same pitch, exported as a two-plane LINEAR
dmabuf. The pass computes each word's address, so the bytes sit where the
consumer is told they are. A driver that cannot export such a buffer keeps
the LINEAR-modifier image of 0035.

punktfunk: also stamps the version banner +pfhdr33.
